# PAM stack of the lock screen: only the password check. The system "login" stack also runs
# pam_faillock / pam_nologin / pam_shells, which an unprivileged process cannot satisfy
# (a correct password came back as a PAM error, and failed tries counted toward an account lockout).
# shortcut: no failure counting here (pam_unix still delays ~2 s per wrong try); set lock.pamService to use a system stack.
auth     required  pam_unix.so
account  required  pam_permit.so
